From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libhexagonrpc: select input sequence type and advance metadata

Preserve the original tested input TYPE_SEQ layout, selecting the descriptor's
own inner type instead of reusing an earlier TYPE or an uninitialized pointer.
Skip the allocated metadata buffer when encoding subsequent arguments; empty
sequences must not consume nonexistent metadata in alloc/encode/free stages.
Validate type indices and keep buffer counts wide until checking the scalar's
eight-bit input/output limit before allocation. Output TYPE_SEQ remains
unqualified and is explicitly refused before consuming pointers or ioctl.

The real C mock-ioctl test checks sequence-first, distinct indices, consecutive
sequences, a following blob, fixed blobs, zero count, invalid tables and count
overflow. Original golden-wire tests are retained unchanged. This does not
establish all IDL families, allocation-failure behavior or hardware operation.

--- a/libhexagonrpc/hexagonrpc.c
